\section{Safety rules}{

\itemize{
\item Every prediction or phone request is sent exactly once. The package
never retries automatically, not even after HTTP 429, a timeout or a lost
response: a request whose response was lost may still have been billed.
\item Redirects are never followed, so the API key is never forwarded to
another host. A 3xx response raises a \code{genderapi_redirect_error}.
\item The default timeout is 10 seconds (see \code{\link[=genderapi_client]{genderapi_client()}}).
\item The base URL must use HTTPS; plain HTTP is accepted only for
\code{localhost}, \verb{127.0.0.1} and \verb{[::1]} (local tests).
\item Loading the package or creating a client never sends a request.
\item The API key is sent only in the \code{Authorization: Bearer} header, never in
a URL, and is never printed. Keep keys on the server; never embed them
in browser code or in documents shared with end users.
}
}

\section{API key and IP trial}{

The key is taken from the \code{api_key} argument of \code{\link[=genderapi_client]{genderapi_client()}} or
from the \code{GENDERAPI_API_KEY} environment variable. Without a key the
server applies its shared IP trial (10 credits per 24 hours for all
clients behind the same public IP); the package does not implement any
trial logic itself. Check \code{meta$access$mode} in every response.
}

